Goalkeeping was of the highest quality in the Champions Trophy final, with both teams ending regulation time at one goal apiece. Argentina's goalkeeper Belen Succi made three successful one-on-one saves after several key saves in the second half to hold the Hockeyroos out.
It took a Kathryn Slattery miscued her shot off an awkward bouncing ball in the 35th minute to break the defences of Succi but Eastham still believes that Australia has the best one-on-one keepers.
"Succi had an incredible game," Eastham said. "She does make a lot of saves and is a key member of the Argentinian team but, to be honest, I think I would back our keepers over her in a one-on-one.
"We did study her approach for the one-on-ones ahead of the job today but I do think Australia has the best one-on-one keepers in the world."
It didn't take long for the hosts to level the scores with Florencia Habif getting her stick on the ball to tip a fiery penalty corner shot past Ashlee Wells in goal.
The Champions Trophy gave Australia an opportunity to blood some young players into international competition before next year's Oceania Cup and the 2016 Olympic Games in Rio de Janeiro.
